{
  "page": 28,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "• The assumptions made should be given (e.g., Normally distributed errors).",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        75.2083740234375,
        459.7899169921875,
        84.11493682861328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• It should be clear whether the error bar is the standard deviation or the standard error",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        88.0733642578125,
        504.1643981933594,
        96.97992706298828
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the mean.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        98.98236083984375,
        213.31507873535156,
        107.88892364501953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• It is OK to report 1-sigma error bars, but one should state it. The authors should",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        111.84637451171875,
        503.999755859375,
        120.75293731689453
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "preferably report a 2-sigma error bar than state that they have a 96% CI, if the hypothesis",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        122.75634765625,
        504.0046691894531,
        131.66290283203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of Normality of errors is not verified.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        133.66534423828125,
        311.67584228515625,
        142.5718994140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• For asymmetric distributions, the authors should be careful not to show in tables or",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        146.52935791015625,
        504.1723937988281,
        155.4368896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "figures symmetric error bars that would yield results that are out of range (e.g. negative",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        157.4393310546875,
        504.0048522949219,
        166.34588623046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "error rates).",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        168.348388671875,
        210.25660705566406,
        177.25494384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• If error bars are reported in tables or plots, The authors should explain in the text how",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        181.21337890625,
        504.357666015625,
        190.11993408203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "they were calculated and reference the corresponding figures or tables in the text.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        192.12237548828125,
        486.9079895019531,
        201.0289306640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Experiments Compute Resources",
      "bbox": [
        131.41200256347656,
        206.8598175048828,
        285.3538818359375,
        215.88592529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Question: For each experiment, does the paper provide sufficient information on the com-",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        221.83636474609375,
        505.6579895019531,
        230.742919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "puter resources (type of compute workers, memory, time of execution) needed to reproduce",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        232.745361328125,
        504.0032958984375,
        241.65191650390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the experiments?",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        243.65533447265625,
        211.50210571289062,
        252.5618896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Answer: [Yes]",
      "bbox": [
        143.5070037841797,
        258.5123291015625,
        201.47940063476562,
        267.41888427734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Justification: We provide the hardware requirements in Appendix A.5.1.",
      "bbox": [
        143.67601013183594,
        273.36932373046875,
        431.2663269042969,
        282.27587890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Guidelines:",
      "bbox": [
        143.8660125732422,
        288.2273254394531,
        189.80357360839844,
        297.1338806152344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The answer NA means that the paper does not include experiments.",
      "bbox": [
        155.32301330566406,
        303.0843200683594,
        432.1935729980469,
        311.9908752441406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The paper should indicate the type of compute workers CPU or GPU, internal cluster,",
      "bbox": [
        155.32301330566406,
        315.9493103027344,
        505.2441711425781,
        324.8559265136719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "or cloud provider, including relevant memory and storage.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        326.8583679199219,
        395.44134521484375,
        335.7649230957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The paper should provide the amount of compute required for each of the individual",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        339.7233581542969,
        503.99713134765625,
        348.6299133300781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "experimental runs as well as estimate the total compute.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        350.6323547363281,
        386.3854064941406,
        359.5389099121094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The paper should disclose whether the full research project required more compute",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        363.4973449707031,
        503.99566650390625,
        372.4039306640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "than the experiments reported in the paper (e.g., preliminary or failed experiments that",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        374.4063720703125,
        503.9959411621094,
        383.31292724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "didn’t make it into the paper).",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        385.31536865234375,
        282.495361328125,
        394.221923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Code Of Ethics",
      "bbox": [
        131.41200256347656,
        400.05279541015625,
        208.6219024658203,
        409.07891845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Question: Does the research conducted in the paper conform, in every respect, with the",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        415.0303649902344,
        504.00213623046875,
        423.9369201660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "NeurIPS Code of Ethics https://neurips.cc/public/EthicsGuidelines?",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        425.9393615722656,
        466.42138671875,
        434.90570068359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Answer: [Yes]",
      "bbox": [
        143.50698852539062,
        440.7963562011719,
        201.47938537597656,
        449.7029113769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Justification: The research conducted in the paper conforms with the NeurIPS Code of",
      "bbox": [
        143.67599487304688,
        455.65435791015625,
        503.9952087402344,
        464.5609130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ethics.",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        466.5633544921875,
        171.26315307617188,
        475.46990966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Guidelines:",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        481.42034912109375,
        189.80355834960938,
        490.326904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The answer NA means that the authors have not reviewed the NeurIPS Code of Ethics.",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        496.2783508300781,
        505.60882568359375,
        505.1849060058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• If the authors answer No, they should explain the special circumstances that require a",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        509.142333984375,
        503.9947814941406,
        518.0488891601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "deviation from the Code of Ethics.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        520.0523681640625,
        301.3446044921875,
        528.9589233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The authors should make sure to preserve anonymity (e.g., if there is a special consid-",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        532.9163818359375,
        505.6539306640625,
        541.8229370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "eration due to laws or regulations in their jurisdiction).",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        543.8253784179688,
        381.2644348144531,
        552.73193359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Broader Impacts",
      "bbox": [
        126.43099975585938,
        558.5637817382812,
        215.9055633544922,
        567.5899047851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Question: Does the paper discuss both potential positive societal impacts and negative",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        573.5403442382812,
        504.0021667480469,
        582.4468994140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "societal impacts of the work performed?",
      "bbox": [
        143.86599731445312,
        584.4493408203125,
        304.512939453125,
        593.3558959960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Answer: [NA]",
      "bbox": [
        143.5070037841797,
        599.307373046875,
        201.02110290527344,
        608.2139282226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Justification: The paper does not address societal impact.",
      "bbox": [
        143.67601013183594,
        614.1643676757812,
        371.1719970703125,
        623.0709228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Guidelines:",
      "bbox": [
        143.8660125732422,
        629.0223388671875,
        189.80357360839844,
        637.9288940429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The answer NA means that there is no societal impact of the work performed.",
      "bbox": [
        155.32301330566406,
        643.8793334960938,
        472.91070556640625,
        652.785888671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• If the authors answer NA or No, they should explain why their work has no societal",
      "bbox": [
        155.32301330566406,
        656.744384765625,
        503.9998779296875,
        665.6509399414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "impact or why the paper does not address societal impact.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        667.6533813476562,
        393.94696044921875,
        676.5599365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• Examples of negative societal impacts include potential malicious or unintended uses",
      "bbox": [
        155.322998046875,
        680.5183715820312,
        503.9949035644531,
        689.4249267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(e.g., disinformation, generating fake profiles, surveillance), fairness considerations",
      "bbox": [
        163.46200561523438,
        691.4273681640625,
        503.9962158203125,
        700.3339233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(e.g., deployment of technologies that could make decisions that unfairly impact specific",
      "bbox": [
        163.46200561523438,
        702.3363647460938,
        503.9979553222656,
        711.242919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "groups), privacy considerations, and security considerations.",
      "bbox": [
        163.79100036621094,
        713.245361328125,
        404.4176025390625,
        722.1519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
